      "id": 1,
      "text": "Alton was originally called \"New Durham Gore\" because of its rocky upland areas and was settled in 1770 by farmers seeking less frost.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alton%2C_New_Hampshire"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was renamed Alton in 1796 after a market town in Hampshire, England.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alton%2C_New_Hampshire"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1847 the Cochecho Railroad brought passengers and freight to Alton Village and Alton Bay, sparking local growth.",
